  "slug": "discovery-database-1f96",
  "summary": "Four November 2026 resources pair larger curated data with predictors, negative sets or graph reasoning for drug discovery, PPI and plant resistance gene analysis.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is established curated resources expanding coverage while adding layers for computational reuse. canSAR 2026 integrates ML predictors, druggability tools and agentic-AI protein tools. HIPPIE 3.0 reaches about 1.2M experimentally supported human PPIs and adds negative training sets, which supports interaction-prediction training. PRGdb 5.0 grows to 874,967 candidate plant resistance proteins and adds DREM deep-learning prioritization. The IDKG preprint takes a different route: it unifies 20 infectious-disease drug discovery sources in a queryable Neo4j graph (4.6M nodes, 26M edges) for graph-based reasoning. The items differ in domain and architecture; the shared pattern is pairing curation or integration with machine-facing, predictive functionality, not a uniform AI component.",
